{"name":"Rio Grande","hex":"#b7c61a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rio Grande","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A major river in the United States and Mexico, starting in Colorado, flowing through New Mexico, and forming the boundary between Texas and the Mexican states of Chihuahua, Coahuila, Nuevo León and Tamaulipas for most of its length.","An unincorporated community and census-designated place in Lower Township and Middle Township, Cape May County, New Jersey, United States, named after the above river."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rio_Grande"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rio Grande","blocks":[{"text":"The Rio Grande, in the United States, or the Río Bravo, in Mexico, also known as Tó Ba'áadi in Navajo, is one of the principal rivers in the Southwestern United States and in northern Mexico. The length of the Rio Grande is 1,896 miles (3,051 km), making it the fourth longest river in the United States and in North America by main stem. It originates in south-central Colorado, in the United States, and flows to the Gulf of Mexico. The Rio Grande drainage basin (watershed) has an area of 182,200 square miles (472,000 km2); however, the endorheic basins that are adjacent to and within the greater drainage basin of the Rio Grande increase the total drainage-basin area to 336,000 square miles (870,000 km2)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Rio_Grande_in_Big_Bend_NP.jpg/330px-Rio_Grande_in_Big_Bend_NP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rio_Grande"},{"title":"Rio Grande (1950 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Rio Grande is a 1950 American romantic Western film directed by John Ford and starring John Wayne and Maureen O'Hara. It is the third installment of Ford's \"Cavalry Trilogy\", following two RKO Pictures releases: Fort Apache (1948) and She Wore a Yellow Ribbon (1949). Wayne plays the lead in all three films, as Captain Kirby York in Fort Apache, then as Captain Nathan Brittles in She Wore a Yellow Ribbon, and finally as a promoted Lieutenant Colonel Kirby Yorke in Rio Grande. Rio Grande's supporting cast features Ben Johnson, Claude Jarman Jr., Harry Carey Jr., Chill Wills, J. Carrol Naish, Victor McLaglen, Grant Withers, the Western singing group the Sons of the Pioneers and Stan Jones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Rio_Grande_poster.jpg/330px-Rio_Grande_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rio_Grande_(1950_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Rio_Grande-2.jpg/500px-Rio_Grande-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Rio_Grande-2.jpg/1280px-Rio_Grande-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Rio_Grande-2.jpg/500px-Rio_Grande-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A riverine islet in the Rio Grande, seen from North Valley, New Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARio_Grande-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Rio_Grande_EP_Upper_Valley.jpg/500px-Rio_Grande_EP_Upper_Valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Rio_Grande_EP_Upper_Valley.jpg/1280px-Rio_Grande_EP_Upper_Valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Rio_Grande_EP_Upper_Valley.jpg/500px-Rio_Grande_EP_Upper_Valley.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rio Grande in west El Paso near the New Mexico stat